  "courseSlug": "javascript-data-structures-and-algorithms",
  "courseTitle": "100 Days of Code: JavaScript Data Structures and Algorithms",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41210360",
      "title": "Tree Terminology",
      "lectureOrder": 129,
      "videoOrder": 128,
      "sourceHash": "35aca6a9211c03b1519ee70fc97d504596e8689034ba8ff087b9586d22e2c792",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 5.27,
          "end": 5.81,
          "en": "All right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.81,
          "end": 10.91,
          "en": "Before continuing to implement the tree data structure, we need to learn the terminology related to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.94,
          "end": 12.02,
          "en": "tree data structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.02,
          "end": 14.42,
          "en": "Here on the right you see a typical tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.42,
          "end": 18.89,
          "en": "And we will start to examine this tree by learning their terminology.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.92,
          "end": 21.29,
          "en": "Now the first terminology over here is root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.29,
          "end": 22.37,
          "en": "So what is root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.37,
          "end": 24.23,
          "en": "It's the top node without parent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.23,
          "end": 30.08,
          "en": "So if we look at this tree over here we can see that each and every node of this tree has a parent except",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.08,
          "end": 31.79,
          "en": "one node which is a top node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.79,
          "end": 33.92,
          "en": "In this case it is n1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.92,
          "end": 36.89,
          "en": "So the root means that this is the top node without any parent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.92,
          "end": 39.29,
          "en": "Now if you check other nodes over here, we can easily see that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.29,
          "end": 42.95,
          "en": "For example for n2 the parent is N1 and for other nodes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.98,
          "end": 45.17,
          "en": "Also there is a parent except n1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.17,
          "end": 47.27,
          "en": "Now the next terminology is edge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.27,
          "end": 50.36,
          "en": "So it's a basically a link between parent and child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.36,
          "end": 53.39,
          "en": "So these lines over here are the edges.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.39,
          "end": 60.17,
          "en": "So if we take for example n2 we can easily see that from n2 we have a children of n4 and n5.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.17,
          "end": 61.58,
          "en": "And there is a link between them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.58,
          "end": 62.75,
          "en": "So this is going to be the edge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.75,
          "end": 65.57,
          "en": "And from N1 we have a children N2 and N3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.57,
          "end": 67.49,
          "en": "These are the edges of this node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.52,
          "end": 69.65,
          "en": "Now the next terminology is leaf.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.68,
          "end": 72.38,
          "en": "A leaf is a node which does not have any children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.41,
          "end": 77.36,
          "en": "So if we look at for example first node over here we can see that for n1 we have two children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.36,
          "end": 82.85,
          "en": "For n2 we have two children which are in four and in five, and for in three we have one children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.85,
          "end": 89.24,
          "en": "So if you go down you see that for N7 and eight and for N6 we don't have any children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.24,
          "end": 92.99000000000001,
          "en": "So this means that these are the leaf of the this tree over here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.99000000000001,
          "end": 95.3,
          "en": "So the next terminology is sibling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.3,
          "end": 97.52000000000001,
          "en": "The sibling is the children of the same parent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.55,
          "end": 102.53,
          "en": "So we can easily see that for example for n2 the children are n4 and n5.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.53,
          "end": 105.68,
          "en": "For n1 the children are n2 and n3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.68,
          "end": 110.3,
          "en": "So if a node has the same parent with the other node, they are sibling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.33,
          "end": 112.4,
          "en": "Now the next terminology is ancestor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.4,
          "end": 114.14,
          "en": "So what is ancestor?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.14,
          "end": 120.74,
          "en": "For a given node, we can easily understand that ancestor is a parent or grandparent or great grandparent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.77,
          "end": 121.31,
          "en": "of the node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.34,
          "end": 127.55,
          "en": "So for example, in case of N7, ancestors are n4 and two and n1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.55,
          "end": 130.91,
          "en": "So these are the ancestors of N7 in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.95,
          "end": 137.94,
          "en": "So if we look at N7, we can easily see that the ancestors of N7 is n4, n2 and n1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.94,
          "end": 141.18,
          "en": "So these three nodes are the ancestors of N7.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.21,
          "end": 144.96,
          "en": "Now the next terminology is that of the node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.96,
          "end": 146.67000000000002,
          "en": "So what's the depth of node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.7,
          "end": 149.82,
          "en": "This is the length of the path from root to this node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.82,
          "end": 156.99,
          "en": "So if for example take this node over here the depth of this node is the length from the root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.99,
          "end": 158.7,
          "en": "So we know that the root is n1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.7,
          "end": 160.41,
          "en": "So it is one and two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.44,
          "end": 163.68,
          "en": "So the depth of this n4 is going to be the two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.71,
          "end": 166.44,
          "en": "Now similarly we can calculate the height of the node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.47,
          "end": 168.48,
          "en": "Now what is the height of node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.51,
          "end": 172.17000000000002,
          "en": "It's a length of the path from the node to the deepest node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.17000000000002,
          "end": 176.61,
          "en": "So if we take for example n3 the height of this n3 is going to be one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.61,
          "end": 181.08,
          "en": "Because from here if we go down we have only one step to the deepest node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.08,
          "end": 183.42,
          "en": "So the height of the N3 is going to be one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.45,
          "end": 189.24,
          "en": "Now if we take for example height of n1 to the deepest node one two, three steps we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.24,
          "end": 193.5,
          "en": "So that's why the height of n1 for example is going to be three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.5,
          "end": 195.6,
          "en": "Now let's continue to the next terminology.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.6,
          "end": 198.55,
          "en": "So the next terminology is depth of the tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.55,
          "end": 201.37,
          "en": "So this is going to be the depth of the root node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.46,
          "end": 205.36,
          "en": "So we know that depth of a given node is a length from path to the root node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.36,
          "end": 208.6,
          "en": "So if we calculate for the root node it's going to be the zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.6,
          "end": 211.21,
          "en": "Because from root node to root node we have zero steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.21,
          "end": 213.31,
          "en": "That's why the depth of tree is going to be zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.34,
          "end": 215.11,
          "en": "Then we have the height of tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.11,
          "end": 217.36,
          "en": "So this is going to be the height of root node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.36,
          "end": 222.64,
          "en": "So we know that height of a node is the length of the path from the node to the deepest node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 222.64,
          "end": 227.71,
          "en": "So in this case height of tree which is height of the root node is going to be three because we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.71,
          "end": 231.19,
          "en": "three steps from m1 to deepest node which is N7.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.19,
          "end": 237.01,
          "en": "So we can take N7 or N8 because both of them are the deepest node from the N1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 237.01,
          "end": 240.46,
          "en": "That's why the height of the tree is going to be three in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 240.46,
          "end": 244.51,
          "en": "So these are the terminologies that you need to know before implementing any tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 244.51,
          "end": 247.96,
          "en": "Because we are going to use these terminologies in our upcoming lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 247.96,
          "end": 250.84,
          "en": "So you have to learn them to understand what we mean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 250.84,
          "end": 254.17,
          "en": "For example when we say edge or root or ancestor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 254.17,
          "end": 259.63,
          "en": "So before implementing the tree data structure we need to know these terminologies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 259.63,
          "end": 261.82,
          "en": "So hopefully everything is clear.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
